Q2.
Near-real-time means data is processed within a few seconds or minutes after it is created.
Example:
Customer places an order at 2:00 PM
Kafka processes it by 2:00:03 PM
Real-time means there is almost zero delay between the event occurring and processing.
So:
Real-time = immediate response
Near-real-time = very small delay (seconds)
